{
 "summary": "Rejected. The URL tooltip is not read the way Java's UrlBuilder reads it: one held-out Java-valid case loses its whole-output match, three tooltip forms differ from Java, and the re-declaration warning fires where Java does not reorder.",
 "findings": [
  "Gains: ck_create_tooltip_legacy matches (created head without its link, ArrowAndParticipant#drawInternalU, plus the {tooltip} title). The maker's tooltip and created-head gains in 790 and 28 reproduce exactly (790: 9 mismatches to match, among others).",
  "LOSS (1 lost match: ck_tooltip_label_brace_legacy): for '[[https://example.org/ring ring{x}]]', Java's UrlBuilder#getUrl alternative S_LINK_WITH_OPTIONAL_TOOLTIP_WITH_OPTIONAL_LABEL reads 'ring{x}' as the label and leaves the tooltip null, so Url#getTooltip is the URL. Java's title is 'https://example.org/ring'; before the change Rust matched. extract_link_tooltip (parse/mod.rs) takes the first '{…}' anywhere in the link, so after the change the title is 'x'.",
  "Divergent (mismatch both before and after, so not a loss): '{ rings }' gives Java title ' rings ' (the [^{}]* group is untrimmed), Rust 'rings'. '{}' gives Java '' (an empty tooltip, not null), Rust the URL. '{a{b}c}' gives Java 'a{b}c' (S_LINK_TOOLTIP_NOLABEL greedy \\{(.+)\\}), Rust 'a{b'. The tooltip needs the five UrlBuilder alternatives in order, not a substring scan.",
  "False warning: ck_redeclare_order_stable_{legacy,teoz} and ck_redeclare_order_lower_legacy are whole-output matches in Java and Rust, yet report_put_participant_in_last warns 'moves ... to last'. SequenceDiagram#putParticipantInLast re-inserts with addWithOrder, before the first participant of strictly greater order, so an explicit order keeps its position. The Rust check compares (order.unwrap_or(index), index) keys, which is right only when every order is the default. The no-order control ck_redeclare_last_legacy is silent and matches, which is correct.",
  "The other new warnings (multiple stereotypes, creole [[link]] in a quoted display, teoz anchors, group COLORS[1]) fire only on AS and 790/28 inputs that mismatch. A single stereotype or a spot stereotype does not warn (checked locally). The AS colour-free controls (note-across, hnote, rnote, teoz box) mismatch silently both before and after, which confirms the maker's claim that the residue is geometry, not colour.",
  "The model change is explained: url_tooltip is additive (2,309 golden, 2,922 retained and 440 fresh AST records add 'url_tooltip: None'); SVG changes only where a {tooltip} exists."
 ],
 "next_obligations": [
  "1 (blocking): port UrlBuilder#getUrl (QUOTED, ONLY_TOOLTIP, ONLY_TOOLTIP_AND_LABEL, LINK_TOOLTIP_NOLABEL, LINK_WITH_OPTIONAL_TOOLTIP_WITH_OPTIONAL_LABEL, in that order, STRICT mode) for participant URLs. The tooltip must be untrimmed and may be empty. Perturbations: ck_tooltip_* plus quoted-URL and tooltip-only forms.",
  "2: report_put_participant_in_last must model addWithOrder (insert before the first strictly greater order) and warn only when the resulting position or box differs. Perturbations: ck_redeclare_order_* plus a reordering explicit-order case."
 ],
